/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch26_cooling_failure / system/controlDict

  WHAT THIS CASE IS: the cooling-failure scenario of thermal process safety
  on a BATCH reactor (DEV.md 4c C60).  A FICTITIOUS exothermic liquid
  reaction, A + B -> P in an inert solvent, is run isothermally at
  T_p = 330 K, held there by a jacket; at the time the recipe declares,
  the jacket stops removing heat and the reactor goes adiabatic with
  whatever B has not yet reacted.  The temperature it
  climbs to is the MAXIMUM TEMPERATURE OF THE SYNTHESIS REACTION (MTSR).

  It is a witness of the EduTool "Process safety" (gui/src/ui/methods/
  ProcessSafetyTool.tsx), which runs it in the browser with the failure
  time moved, and with `value 0` (no failure) to draw the accumulation of
  normal operation.

  WHAT IS MEASURED AND WHAT IS NOT: nothing here is validated against a
  measured reactor, and nothing could be: the substances are fictitious,
  every property an author-set teaching assumption (see constant/reactions
  and constant/components/), and the adiabatic leg is a closed liquid with no
  vapour phase, so temperatures above the mixture's boiling point are the
  hypothetical the methodology asks for, not what a vented vessel would
  do.  Narrative: system/flowsheetDict header.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoBatch;
description   "Cooling failure on a batch (fictitious A + B -> P in solvent S): isothermal at 330 K, the jacket stops at t_f, the accumulated B drives T to T_cf";

verbosity     2;

// ---- Time integration ----
startTime       0;        // s
endTime         6000;     // s   (100 min: at 330 K the batch is ~95 % converted in an hour)
deltaT          0.5;      // s   (the adiabatic leg reaches ~405 K, where k ~ 0.1 1/s)
writeInterval   50;       // s   (one trajectory row per 50 s)

//  No <t>/ time directories: the trajectory is what this case is read by,
//  and a restart from the middle of the scenario is not its question.
solutionControl
{
    write       false;
}
